0..78 Comment "// Located judgements over the seat exchange: an operator dispatches work to a"
79..156 Comment "// seat, the seat works where it stands, and what comes back is a report or a"
157..234 Comment "// handle to one. The judgement `M : A @ w` reads a term at a world; `A at w`"
235..310 Comment "// is a handle to a value at `w`, `hold` makes one at the current world and"
311..384 Comment "// `let x at w` opens one at `w`; `migrate [w] { M }` runs `M` at `w` and"
385..460 Comment "// spends one capability `cap_w` the entry holds (Murphy, Crary and Harper,"
461..539 Comment "// \"Type-Safe Distributed Programming with ML5\", TGC 2007, §3: `get`, `hold`,"
540..551 Comment "// `leta`)."
552..626 Comment "// Only what is mobile and open comes back: a `mobile type` component of a"
627..679 Comment "// sealed signature says its representation crosses."
681..755 Comment "// The seat\'s protocol and its messages, sealed, its report marked mobile."
756..762 Keyword "import"
